  "source_type": "literature",
  "citation": "Turlin et al. Core and auxiliary functions of one-carbon metabolism in Pseudomonas putida exposed by a systems-level analysis of transcriptional and physiological responses. mSystems (2023). DOI: 10.1128/msystems.00004-23. [PMC10308882]",
  "doi": "10.1128/msystems.00004-23",
  "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10308882/",
  "notes": "Extracted from the primary paper (snippet: DBM medium contained 3.88 g L−1 K2HPO4, 1.63 g L−1 NaH2PO4, 2 g L−1 (NH4)2SO4, and 0.1 g L−1 MgCl2·6H2O, with the initial pH adjusted at 7.0. DBM medium was supplemented with a trace element solution ). Component names mapped to BiGG (see mapping_confidence); presence-based bounds unless the paper gave exchange bounds; concentration_mM where units allowed. Extraction confidence: high.",
  "verification": "paper-verified (complete recipe; cited + supplementary sources chased)",
  "verification_evidence": "DBM medium contained 3.88 g L−1 K2HPO4",
  "verification_confidence": "high",
  "base_medium": "de Bont minimal medium (DBM), Hartmans/de Bont mineral medium",
  "recuration": {
   "date": "2026-07-16",
   "round": "complete-recipe (cited+supplementary chased)",
   "status": "confirmed",
   "confidence": "high",
   "sources_chased": [
    {
     "what": "base medium cited as ref 34 (Hartmans, Smits, van der Werf, Volkering, de Bont 1989, Appl Environ Microbiol 55:2850-2855, PMC203180, doi:10.1128/aem.55.11.2850-2855.1989)",
     "obtained": false,
     "how": "WebFetch of PMC203180 HTML and PDF returned only abstract/download-shell (methods not text-extractable); full DBM recipe including complete trace-element solution is already spelled out verbatim in the main text of PMC10308882, so no additional constituents were recoverable or needed",
     "added": []
    }
   ],
   "missing_before": [],
   "corrections": [],
   "notes": "The paper's main text gives the DBM recipe in full: phosphate buffer (K2HPO4 + NaH2PO4), (NH4)2SO4 as N/S source, MgCl2·6H2O, and the complete de Bont trace-element solution (EDTA chelator + Zn, Ca, Fe, Mo, Cu, Co, Mn salts). DBM is a defined medium requiring no vitamins/growth factors for P. putida; none are added. Standard carbon source is 20 mM glucose (methanol and formate are experiment-specific supplements, not part of the base medium). Cultivations are aerobic (P. putida is an obligate aerobe). All element exchanges in current_components are covered; concentrations and exact salt identi"
  },
